      "content": "but that's the thing, i don't want to \"heal.\" healing implies there's actually something underneath all this damage to save. but there isn't. it feels like the foundation is just gone. isn't it possible that some things are just too damaged to ever be whole again? like, why keep trying to patch up something that's fundamentally destroyed?",
